<title>USA: Lafarge, Laidlaw end unit sale negotiation.</title>
<headline>Lafarge, Laidlaw end unit sale negotiation.</headline>
<dateline>RESTON, Va. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lafarge Corp said talks with Laidlaw Inc about buying Laidlaw's JTM Industries Inc unit terminated without a deal.</p>
<p>The companies announced April 29 they were discussing the sale of the unit, which specializes in recycling fly ash, a fossil-fuel by-product.</p>
<p>&quot;As we went through the process, we couldn't agree on all the terms and conditions,&quot; a company spokesman said in a telephone interview.</p>
